☐ [Phase 1 - Split Contract and Baseline] Freeze the behavior-preserving DwarfUICore extraction boundary and capture reproducible evidence before moving files.
    ☐ Record the current DwarfUI repository path, branch, status, index state, source package version, and installed runtime path without stashing, committing, or altering unrelated changes.
    ☐ Inventory every production module, test, fixture, tool, document, and package entry involved in tooltip, context-menu, pointer, widget-extension, projection, root-discovery, and shared runtime behavior.
    ☐ Produce a transitive dependency map beginning at `dwarfui/tooltip/api`, `dwarfui/context_menu/api`, and their runtime owners.
    ☐ Classify every dependency as DwarfUICore-owned, DwarfUI-owned, temporarily bridged during extraction, or retained as an external DFHack dependency.
    ☐ Confirm that DwarfUICore will be a standalone sibling repository at `D:\CODE\DFHack\DwarfUICore`, not a nested checkout, submodule, subtree, or vendored directory.
    ☐ Fix the project identifiers: repository `DwarfUICore`, mod ID `dwarfuicore`, LuaRocks package `dwarfuicore`, root script `dwarfuicore`, LuaDoc namespace `dwarfuicore`, and process-state root `dfhack.dwarfuicore`.
    ☐ Define the extraction rule: preserve current service behavior and public operations; do not implement providers, consumer namespaces, composite identities, contract-major negotiation, immutable API objects, or the proposed new collision rules.
    ☐ Identify every behavior change that would be tempting during the move and defer it to the still-unfinalized service-provider proposal.
    ☐ Record current focused unit, full unit, syntax, package, archive, and available live-test results as separate baseline evidence.
    ☐ Record pre-existing failures and unavailable live prerequisites without treating them as split regressions.
    Deliverables:
    - Approved source-and-test ownership inventory.
    - Transitive dependency map with no unclassified module.
    - Explicit behavior-preservation and deferral list.
    - Baseline evidence report separated by test category.

☐ [Phase 2 - Standalone Repository Bootstrap] Establish DwarfUICore as an independently buildable local project while preserving relevant history.
    ☐ Create the sibling `DwarfUICore` working directory from DwarfUI history using a history-preserving split mechanism.
    ☐ Ensure the new checkout does not remain connected to the DwarfUI remote as a writable destination.
    ☐ Decide the DwarfUICore remote owner, visibility, default branch, and release destination before creating external state.
    ☐ Obtain explicit authorization before creating or pushing a new remote repository.
    ☐ Configure the approved DwarfUICore remote as `origin` and verify no push URL targets the DwarfUI repository.
    ☐ Retain only extracted infrastructure history, relevant test infrastructure, build tools, license, and documentation history needed by DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Create `src/info.txt` with mod ID `dwarfuicore`, name `DwarfUICore`, initial package version, compatibility metadata, author, description, and DFHack tags.
    ☐ Create `dwarfuicore.rockspec` with the correct package identity, source location, Lua version, runtime dependencies, and DwarfSpec test dependency.
    ☐ Create `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.gitignore`, `.luarc.json`, `.busted`, environment example, and editor workspace configuration appropriate to the new project.
    ☐ Copy and rename the project-local `tools/` scripts so DwarfUICore can build, test, publish, and verify its package without invoking DwarfUI tooling.
    ☐ Ensure every tool resolves paths relative to the DwarfUICore repository and uses mod ID `dwarfuicore` for explicit live reload.
    ☐ Add `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfuicore.lua` as a `--@ module=true` command/module entrypoint with current-generation validation and explicit development reload behavior.
    ☐ Add a DwarfUICore module registry and an initial package-contract test.
    ☐ Run foundation syntax, focused unit, full unit, and package checks independently.
    Deliverables:
    - Standalone local DwarfUICore repository.
    - Independently runnable build, test, publish, and package-verification tools.
    - Initial valid DwarfUICore package structure.

☐ [Phase 3 - Shared Infrastructure Extraction] Move the reusable prerequisites required by tooltip and context-menu systems without redesigning their contracts.
    ☐ Move and rename the class-model helper required by current service validation.
    ☐ Move and rename numeric, immutable-enum, function-chain, text, and other utilities required transitively by the extracted systems.
    ☐ Move and rename map projection, pointer dispatch, pointer polling, root resolution, and widget-extension infrastructure.
    ☐ Rename production paths from `dwarfui/...` to `dwarfuicore/...` inside DwarfUICore-owned modules.
    ☐ Rename LuaDoc types from `dwarfui.*` to `dwarfuicore.*` only for types now owned by DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Start every moved production module with `--@ module=true` and load project modules only with `reqscript('dwarfuicore/...')`.
    ☐ Add LuaDoc comments for every moved or changed class and function.
    ☐ Preserve immutable numeric enums for all existing closed discriminator sets.
    ☐ Add every moved module to the DwarfUICore registry in dependency order and update registry/package tests.
    ☐ Move the corresponding focused tests and fixtures, changing only repository paths, module names, LuaDoc ownership, and test harness dependencies needed by the split.
    ☐ Preserve current pointer, projection, root-discovery, and widget-extension behavior exactly.
    ☐ Verify repeated same-generation loads preserve current process-owned state and widget contracts.
    ☐ Run focused infrastructure tests, full DwarfUICore unit tests, syntax checks, and package verification separately.
    Deliverables:
    - Core-owned shared prerequisite modules.
    - Moved tests proving behavior parity.
    - No production dependency from DwarfUICore back to DwarfUI.

☐ [Phase 4 - Tooltip System Extraction] Move the current tooltip system into DwarfUICore without introducing the proposed provider or namespace architecture.
    ☐ Move and rename tooltip target, detector, map-target, service, registration, render-hook, renderer, presenter, runtime, and API modules.
    ☐ Preserve the existing `register`, `unregister`, `register_map_tile`, `update_map_tile`, `unregister_map_tile`, and diagnostics operations.
    ☐ Preserve current widget and map-registration identity, weak lifetime, eligibility, ordering, intent, presentation, polling, and hook semantics.
    ☐ Preserve one process-wide tooltip service, presenter, poller, detector, render-hook manager, and registration state.
    ☐ Move tooltip process state from `dfhack.dwarfui` to the DwarfUICore-owned state root without resetting healthy state during normal repeated loads.
    ☐ Ensure ordinary `reqscript` loading never invokes development reload or clears script environments.
    ☐ Rename internal paths and LuaDoc ownership without publishing internal prerequisites as a new consumer contract.
    ☐ Move generic tooltip tests and fixtures to DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Add extraction regressions for cold load, repeated load, singleton preservation, registration preservation, map-handle behavior, diagnostics, partial state, and explicit reload.
    ☐ Run focused tooltip tests, full DwarfUICore tests, syntax checks, package verification, and focused live tooltip evidence separately.
    Deliverables:
    - DwarfUICore-owned tooltip system with current behavior preserved.
    - One process-wide tooltip runtime.
    - Unit, package, and focused live parity evidence.

☐ [Phase 5 - Context-Menu System Extraction] Move the current context-menu system into DwarfUICore without introducing provider, namespace, or menu-composition redesigns.
    ☐ Move and rename context-menu definition, target, root-discovery, map-target, registration, input-sample, detector, input-hook, service, renderer, screen, and API modules.
    ☐ Preserve the existing `register`, `update`, `unregister`, `register_map_tile`, `update_map_tile`, `unregister_map_tile`, and diagnostics operations.
    ☐ Preserve current widget and map-registration identity, replacement, eligibility, detection, input, failure containment, presentation, and selection semantics.
    ☐ Preserve one process-wide context-menu registration manager, root-discovery owner, input-hook manager, service, presentation owner, and screen lifecycle.
    ☐ Move context-menu process state from `dfhack.dwarfui` to the DwarfUICore-owned state root without changing current deliberate reload cleanup behavior.
    ☐ Ensure ordinary `reqscript` loading never invokes development reload or clears script environments.
    ☐ Rename internal paths and LuaDoc ownership without publishing internal prerequisites as a new consumer contract.
    ☐ Move generic context-menu tests and fixtures to DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Add extraction regressions for cold load, repeated load, singleton preservation, registration preservation, map-handle behavior, callback containment, diagnostics, partial state, and explicit reload.
    ☐ Run focused context-menu tests, full DwarfUICore tests, syntax checks, package verification, and focused live context-menu evidence separately.
    Deliverables:
    - DwarfUICore-owned context-menu system with current behavior preserved.
    - One process-wide context-menu runtime.
    - Unit, package, and focused live parity evidence.

☐ [Phase 6 - DwarfUICore Development Lifecycle] Give the extracted project an explicit reload boundary while keeping consumer initialization non-destructive.
    ☐ Move current shared-runtime validation and module-registry reload responsibilities from `dwarfui.lua` into `dwarfuicore.lua`.
    ☐ Implement `dwarfuicore reload` as the only command that clears DwarfUICore-managed script environments and rebuilds Core modules.
    ☐ Preserve current dependency-safe teardown and reload ordering for tooltip and context-menu runtime owners.
    ☐ Ensure `reqscript('dwarfuicore')` as a module performs no reload, teardown, environment clearing, or overlay rescan.
    ☐ Ensure repeated normal API imports reuse healthy singleton state and registrations.
    ☐ Keep DwarfUICore reload behavior explicit and development-only; do not expose it through tooltip or context-menu APIs.
    ☐ Detect and report missing registry entries, missing files, malformed module contracts, partial service state, and failed reload reconstruction clearly.
    ☐ Add focused tests for validation, repeated validation, explicit reload, failed reload, teardown order, and absence of destructive work during normal loading.
    Deliverables:
    - Independent `dwarfuicore` validation and explicit reload command.
    - Non-destructive normal import behavior.
    - Lifecycle regression coverage.

☐ [Phase 7 - DwarfUI Cutover] Convert DwarfUI into a consumer of the extracted current APIs and remove duplicate Core ownership.
    ☐ Add an explicit DwarfUICore development and package dependency to DwarfUI.
    ☐ Add DwarfUICore public/current API definitions to DwarfUI's LuaLS workspace without treating arbitrary Core internals as DwarfUI modules.
    ☐ Replace DwarfUI production imports of moved modules with their `dwarfuicore/...` paths.
    ☐ Update DwarfUI tooltip and context-menu registrations for minecart markers, mood UI, hover-action rails, and other feature integrations without changing observable behavior.
    ☐ Retain DwarfUI-owned widgets, popovers, hotkeys, feature models, and overlay entrypoints in DwarfUI.
    ☐ Update the DwarfUI module registry to remove every moved Core module and preserve dependency order among the remaining feature modules.
    ☐ Remove DwarfUI's duplicate tooltip, context-menu, pointer, widget-extension, hook, presenter, screen, registration, and service implementations only after all DwarfUI imports have migrated.
    ☐ Remove DwarfUI-owned process-state slots that were transferred to `dfhack.dwarfuicore` without clearing the live DwarfUICore owners during normal initialization.
    ☐ Change `dwarfui reload` so it reloads only DwarfUI-owned modules and overlays and never invokes `dwarfuicore reload`.
    ☐ Ensure DwarfUI overlay retirement unregisters or releases only resources those overlays currently own under the existing APIs.
    ☐ Update DwarfUI tests and fixtures to resolve the separately owned DwarfUICore modules.
    ☐ Keep generic tooltip, context-menu, pointer, and lifecycle tests in DwarfUICore; DwarfUI tests assert only feature integration behavior.
    ☐ Do not modify DwarfDirect, DwarfSearch, or any other independent consumer plugin.
    Deliverables:
    - DwarfUI consuming separately packaged DwarfUICore modules.
    - No duplicate Core implementation or process owner in DwarfUI.
    - DwarfUI reload isolated from DwarfUICore reload.

☐ [Phase 8 - Cross-Project Development and Package Integration] Establish reproducible resolution across two independent repositories and packages.
    ☐ Add both sibling repositories to the development workspace without nesting either Git checkout.
    ☐ Define a reproducible DwarfUI test dependency source for DwarfUICore; do not silently consume whichever sibling files happen to be present.
    ☐ Keep DwarfUICore unit tests self-contained and keep DwarfUI feature tests explicit about whether they use doubles, source modules, expanded packages, or installed runtime modules.
    ☐ Add a controlled integration setup that installs the intended DwarfUICore package before DwarfUI live tests.
    ☐ Record the resolved `dwarfuicore` script path, installed package version, source identity, and sibling checkout identity in integration evidence.
    ☐ Detect stale or duplicate installed DwarfUICore copies before interpreting live failures.
    ☐ Make the DwarfUICore package contain `info.txt`, `dwarfuicore.lua`, all registered Core modules, and no DwarfUI feature files.
    ☐ Make the DwarfUI package contain no `dwarfuicore.lua`, `dwarfuicore/` modules, or duplicate Core implementation.
    ☐ Update both module-registry and package-contract suites for their final ownership boundaries.
    ☐ Verify source, expanded package, and zip manifests by relative path and content hash for both projects.
    ☐ Inspect both final archives directly after publishing.
    ☐ Install DwarfUICore first, then DwarfUI, and prove DwarfUI resolves the intended Core package.
    ☐ Verify missing, partial, incompatible, and stale installed DwarfUICore copies fail clearly enough to diagnose the package boundary.
    Deliverables:
    - Reproducible two-repository development configuration.
    - Separately publishable and verifiable packages.
    - Installed script-resolution evidence.

☐ [Phase 9 - Documentation and Proposal Handoff] Document the completed split and transfer the unfinished architecture proposal to its owning repository.
    ☐ Document DwarfUICore installation, current module entrypoints, explicit reload command, package compatibility, and DwarfUI dependency order.
    ☐ Document DwarfUICore as the owner of reusable tooltip, context-menu, pointer, registration, and presentation infrastructure.
    ☐ Update DwarfUI documentation to describe DwarfUI as a feature/component library that depends on DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Remove stale DwarfUI documentation that claims ownership of moved Core internals while retaining accurate feature-integration documentation.
    ☐ Copy `Docs/service-provider-api-proposal.md` into the DwarfUICore repository as a proposed, unimplemented architecture document.
    ☐ Update proposal paths and project terminology so future design work occurs entirely within DwarfUICore.
    ☐ Mark every provider, namespace, composite-identity, exact-contract-version, immutable-handle, and new collision rule as not implemented by the repository split.
    ☐ Do not create `dwarfuicore-service-provider.todo` until the architecture proposal is finalized and explicitly approved.
    ☐ Leave an appropriate pointer in DwarfUI documentation to the DwarfUICore-owned proposal instead of maintaining divergent copies.
    ☐ Document that migration of independent consumer plugins is separate future work.
    Deliverables:
    - Accurate DwarfUICore and DwarfUI ownership documentation.
    - One canonical unimplemented service-provider proposal in DwarfUICore.
    - No premature service-provider implementation checklist.

☐ [Phase 10 - Final Split Verification] Prove that DwarfUICore is independently healthy and DwarfUI consumes it without duplicated ownership or architectural redesign.
    ☐ Run DwarfUICore focused infrastructure, tooltip, context-menu, lifecycle, registry, and package-contract tests.
    ☐ Run the complete DwarfUICore unit suite.
    ☐ Run DwarfUICore production and test syntax checks.
    ☐ Publish and verify the DwarfUICore package, then inspect its archive.
    ☐ Run focused native DwarfUICore tooltip and context-menu parity tests with cleanup confirmed.
    ☐ Run DwarfUI focused Core-consumer, feature-integration, reload-isolation, registry, and package-contract tests.
    ☐ Run the complete DwarfUI unit suite.
    ☐ Run DwarfUI production and test syntax checks.
    ☐ Publish and verify the DwarfUI package, then inspect its archive for absence of Core implementation files.
    ☐ Run focused native DwarfUI feature tests against the installed DwarfUICore package with cleanup confirmed.
    ☐ Verify cold start with DwarfUICore and DwarfUI installed, repeated current API imports, singleton preservation, registration preservation, DwarfUI reload isolation, and explicit Core reload behavior.
    ☐ Reconcile all results against the Phase 1 baseline and classify every difference as intended path/ownership movement, fixed defect, pre-existing failure, or regression.
    ☐ Audit both repositories for unresolved placeholders, obsolete imports, duplicate runtime owners, stale documentation, and unexpected generated or packaged files.
    ☐ Confirm unrelated pre-existing worktree and index changes remain preserved in both repositories.
    ☐ Confirm that no independent consumer plugin was modified.
    ☐ Confirm that provider construction, namespaces, composite identities, exact service-contract negotiation, immutable service APIs, and proposed new cross-namespace behavior remain unimplemented.
    ☐ Record separate final outcomes for focused tests, full tests, syntax, package verification, archive inspection, installed resolution, native behavior, cleanup, and unavailable evidence.
    Completion gate:
    - DwarfUICore builds, tests, packages, installs, validates, and explicitly reloads independently.
    - DwarfUI imports moved current APIs from DwarfUICore and contains no duplicate Core runtime implementation.
    - Exactly one current tooltip runtime and one current context-menu runtime exist process-wide.
    - Normal imports preserve singleton services and registrations and never perform development reload or clear script environments.
    - DwarfUI reload does not reload or clear DwarfUICore.
    - Current observable tooltip and context-menu behavior matches the pre-split baseline except for approved project/module ownership changes.
    - The unfinalized service-provider proposal is owned by DwarfUICore and remains explicitly unimplemented.
    - All required documentation and verification evidence are complete.
